{"id":1742751,"retrievedAt":"2026-08-04T13:23:33.368Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/XX2G6oEFcwudoEmHJ5HzqFPUjU.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"},{"id":18,"name":"Drama"},{"id":10751,"name":"Family"}],"homepage":"https://sweet16film.com/","id":1742751,"imdb_id":"tt2403682","origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Sweet 16","overview":"November 14th 2007, the UN declares diabetes a worldwide epidemic, launching an annual global awareness event, World Diabetes Day. On that day, 16-year-old filmmaker Katia from Montreal began a journey now called \"Sweet 16\", chronicling Katia's highs and lows; as she and her father/filmmaker turn the lens on a disease that currently touches over 300 million people globally.  Sweet 16 offers a fresh perspective into a silent killer, with a focus on teen issues of body image, peer pressure, in the context of this increasingly prevalent disease. But Sweet is not a medical documentary. Part road movie, part filmed diary, Sweet 16 is a frank human portrayal of what it takes to challenge health issues during critical rites of passage into adulthood.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/zkL0uYfatUyzkpxYQ3buiEN6ubX.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"2012-08-27","revenue":0,"runtime":78,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"A journey into teen Diabetes","title":"Sweet 16","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"crew":[]},"external_ids":{"imdb_id":"tt2403682","wikidata_id":null,"facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"images":{"backdrops":[{"aspect_ratio":1.778,"height":1080,"iso_3166_1":null,"iso_639_1":null,"file_path":"/XX2G6oEFcwudoEmHJ5HzqFPUjU.jpg","vote_average":3.334,"vote_count":1,"width":1920},{"aspect_ratio":1.778,"height":1080,"iso_3166_1":null,"iso_639_1":null,"file_path":"/lKqJypGrQdCy6L9NK9BO9Bf